-- It stops voice input and file uploads, including dropped or pasted files, and asks you first ("Allow once"), because it cannot check them. When it stops a file, its message shows the file's name. The name is shown in TDS's own message on your screen; it is not stored and not sent.
+- **Text files** (.txt, .md, .csv, up to 1 MB): when you paste, drop or attach one, the TDS extension reads it on your device, masks what it finds, checks the copy again, and attaches the masked copy, named "masked-by-TDS.txt" (or .md, .csv), instead of the original. A file in which it finds nothing is attached as it is, with Autopilot on; with Autopilot off, it asks first. If the site takes no file from TDS, the masked text goes into the chat box. With Autopilot off, it asks first: "Attach masked copy", "Allow once" (the original, for 30 seconds) or "Cancel".
+- **Other files** (PDF, Word, images and others), text files over 1 MB or not in UTF-8, and voice input are not checked. It stops them and asks first ("Allow once"). When it stops a file, its message shows the file's name. The name is shown in TDS's own message on your screen; it is not stored and not sent.
+- The file's content is read in memory and is not stored by the TDS extension. The real values behind the placeholders go into the same session list as typed text, and are gone when you close the browser.
+- **A limit:** the site may not take the masked copy TDS hands it. The message asks you to check that the file shows before you send. The same detection limits apply: names in running text are only partly found.
